{"name":"Rich Brown","hex":"#715e4f","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rich","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wealthy: having a lot of money and possessions.","Having an intense fatty or sugary flavour."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The rich people of a society or the world collectively, the rich class of a society.","(Can we verify this sense?)  the second placer in Tycoon"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rich"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rich Brown (blues musician)","blocks":[{"text":"Richard Brown, also known as Uncle Rich Brown, was an American musician and singer of spirituals and blues. He lived on one plantation near Sumterville, Alabama, all his life. John Lomax recorded him in 1937 and 1940 singing eleven songs, most of them spirituals. One of his most popular recordings was \"Alabama Bound\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/John-avery-lomax1_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-John-avery-lomax1_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rich_Brown_(blues_musician)","wikidata":"Q27835038"},{"title":"Rich Brown (Michigan politician)","blocks":[{"text":"Rich Brown is the former clerk, former assistant clerk, and former Democratic member of the Michigan House of Representatives."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rich_Brown_(Michigan_politician)","wikidata":"Q25753443"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":